Z||000016||JSocha||05-22-2001||12:46 AM||||Hey Lisa, just read the thread you had referred to.<P>Seems like a lot of people were there on your side, supporting you.<P>Just food for thought.<P>I would hate to see you leave because of misconceptions by others.  Remember, that with this type of communicaiton vehicle, one lacks the visual and emotional feedback (that one would get if face to face), therefore misconceptions are going to be higher then what was originally intended.<P>I have always cherished your posts, your witty comebacks, your humor on these threads as well as your wisdom on Fiero's.<P>Jelouse?  You bet you!  Someone could sell me a "muffler bearing" and I would be first in line and non the wiser.  How many gals do you know out there, without the nickname "Sam", that know anything about cars more then what you do?  You got me beat just by picking up a wrench, that's how automotively challenged I am.<P>Regarding the trophy (haven't found your thread and picture yet with it...but will continue to look as I would like to see your your recent win at the show), its your trophy.  You worked hard for it and if others are jelouse, that shows there maturity level.  If the words in your comment, as its only words, that the others have taken to personally, then that is there problem, not yours.  Ignore them even if it does hurt as the others that stand behind you will also assist in defending you when you don't speak, as I noticed they did in the last post to keep some if any of the "jerks" in line.  Perhaps me one day when I get out of line.<P>Guys and as a newbie here, I think those of you should just put this matter to rest and those that feel they owe Lisa perhaps some words of apology should take the time to email her personally off this thread and take some responsibility for their words if not actions.  It appears to me Lisa had in the previous post.<P>It shouldn't be the woman that always has to say "their sorry".  Once in awhile we as guys are allowed to bend a little and need to to keep life in balance, especially if we were the ones out of line.<P>Again Lisa, I sincerely hope you will stay with the rest of us and all your friends that you have come to know (I still was getting to know you both here and off line regarding the horses), as I know they will stand behind you through the thickest of times.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
